PRE-TABLE CHECK -- armbdt
Written BEFORE table 1 runs, so this file's own mtime proves the order.

THE DIFF UNDER TEST is in src/cpus/cpu_arm_instr.c:
  arm_pop() (:1653) and arm_push() (:1842):
    Masking `addr & ~3` strictly at the two memory_rw call sites:
      if (!cpu->memory_rw(cpu, cpu->mem, addr & ~3, data, sizeof(data), MEM_READ, CACHE_DATA))
      if (!cpu->memory_rw(cpu, cpu->mem, addr & ~3, data, sizeof(data), MEM_WRITE, CACHE_DATA))
  NEVER masking at function entry, preserving unmasked arithmetic writeback (*np = addr).

--------------------------------------------------------------------- SIBLING PARITY

1. In-tree multi-generator precedent:
   src/cpus/generate_arm_multi.c:117 emits `addr &= 0xffc;` on access before host page indexing,
   while writeback derivation uses the unmasked arithmetic base register.
2. Single-register load/store precedent (#19, #357, #364):
   cpu_arm_instr_loadstore.c separates access masking from base register writeback.
   ARM DDI 0100I A5.2.5 / A5.2.8 / A4-37 specifies that LDM/STM ignore addr[1:0] on memory
   access while Mode 4 writeback updates Rn with unmasked arithmetic offset.

--------------------------------------------------------------------- CLAIM -> ROW

1. "Unaligned base splices bytes across word boundary on cold host pages (arm_pop/LDM)"
   -> ROWED as ARM_LDM_COLD_DATA, ARM_LDM_DIV_CHECK (fails pre-fix, passes post-fix).
2. "Cold LDM pre-fix produces specific predictable byte pattern (attribution)"
   -> ROWED as CONTROL_ATTRIB_PLUS1 (asserts cold unaligned load at 0x20001 yields 0x88112233).
3. "Unaligned base splices bytes across word boundary on cold host pages (arm_push/STM)"
   -> ROWED as ARM_STM_COLD_DATA, ARM_STM_DIV_CHECK (fails pre-fix, passes post-fix).
4. "Cold STM pre-fix corrupts adjacent byte at 0x21004"
   -> ROWED as ARM_STM_COLD_CLOBBER (asserts word 1 byte at 0x21004 clobbered by 0x11 pre-fix).
5. "Thumb POP inherits the defect (cpu_arm.c:1677 -> arm_pop)"
   -> ROWED as THUMB_POP_COLD_DATA, THUMB_POP_DIV_CHECK (fails pre-fix, passes post-fix).
6. "Thumb PUSH inherits the defect (cpu_arm.c:1670 -> arm_push)"
   -> ROWED as THUMB_PUSH_COLD_DATA, THUMB_PUSH_DIV_CHECK (fails pre-fix, passes post-fix).
7. "Mandatory writeback: base register equals unmasked arithmetic result (kills mask-at-entry mutant)"
   -> ROWED as ARM_LDM_WB_UNAL1, ARM_LDM_WB_UNAL2, ARM_STM_WB_UNAL, THUMB_POP_WB_UNAL, THUMB_PUSH_WB_UNAL.
8. "Liveness control: aligned round-trip passes"
   -> ROWED as CONTROL_LIVENESS.
9. "Path assertions: cold access is genuinely cold, warm access is genuinely resident"
   -> ROWED as ARM_LDM_PATH_COLD, ARM_LDM_PATH_WARM, ARM_STM_PATH_COLD, ARM_STM_PATH_WARM.

